  "root_cause_and_fix": [
    "The old UnitApplier/Recomposer/runCurrent fixtures drained their own test scheduler without joining persistent GlobalSnapshotManager apply notifications. sendApplyNotifications does not await callbacks already captured by another thread.",
    "The earlier two-write patch synchronized selectedLanguage writes but left the production provider's internal appliedLanguageTag effect write global. The RTL sibling retained the primary write race.",
    "Both tests now use public runSkikoComposeUiTest real-scene ownership, autoAdvance=true by default, runOnIdle mutations and subsequent waitForIdle. Pinned ui-test1.10.3 isIdle336–350 checks pending snapshot changes, in-flight notification count and scene invalidations, so it accounts for both paths.",
    "A320x640 framebuffer bounds the small fixture's rendering cost. Explicit60-second timeout preserves the original deadline rather than accepting the Skiko API's infinite default. No sleeps, speculative snapshot calls, retries, disabled assertions, remount key or production workaround were added."
  ],
  "assertion_review": {
    "initial_loading": "Ordered SideEffect records assert first Loading, final Content, nonempty loading observations and empty text during all loading observations. This preserves the old immediate-loading requirement despite public setContent waiting off the UI thread.",
    "language_and_state": "Actual Leave -> مغادرة -> Leave resources, ar -> en-US locale, stable remembered object, zero intermediate disposal and no repeated loading during switches are asserted.",
    "system_basis": "Initial default is Locale.US. English effect saves US/installs en; disposal restores US before Arabic saves US/installs ar; Arabic disposal restores US before null/System uses US unchanged. The en-US and final Locale.US assertions follow the actual Desktop provider ownership.",
    "teardown": "The public scene closes/disposes and drains scheduled foreground events in its finally. Successful fixture asserts exactly one content disposal and Locale.US; unconditional outer finally restores the original process locale even if assertions/teardown fail.",
    "rtl": "Both complete RenderedFormatting expectations remain: LTR English middle-dot separator, RTL Arabic comma separator, and unchanged bullet/timer formatting. Locale and selectedLanguage mutate together on UI thread; idle follows outside callback. Source-call-site punctuation test/root-search/regex are unchanged.",
    "discovery": "Both replaced methods use Unit/void block bodies with unchanged kotlin.test.Test names/annotations. Raw XML contains all3 descriptors from changed files and zero skipped cases.",
    "regression_boundaries": "No production state, settings, navigation, resources, game rules, protocol, host authority, private projection, snapshot format, content identity/version or dependency changes."
  },
  "counter_evidence": [
    "runOnIdle waits before callback, not after; every mutation here has an explicit subsequent waitForIdle outside the UI thread callback.",
    "Neither fixture disables autoAdvance; its false branch would bypass snapshot/recomposer idle checks.",
    "Desktop resources use synchronous remember/runBlocking; no asynchronous-I/O explanation is invented.",
    "Initial loading and retained-state/disposal assertions were not replaced with final-text-only checks; a force-remount fix would fail the retained state tests.",
    "The fixed test harness does not establish any new production locale defect or iOS/Android preference behavior."
  ],
